      <Comment source="O-28, pujar">The P450 monoxygenase CYP93G2 was analyzed by recombinant enzyme assays and with transgenic arabidopsis and in a CYP93G2 T-DNA insertion mutant rice |CITS: [20647377]|. The expressed protein is closely related to Sorghum CYP93G3 with 69.7% sequence identity, has 518 amino acids with a signature sequences of a pro hinge region, an oxygen-binding pocket and a heme-binding motif of P450 enzymes.</Comment>
